8","y":"128"},"Opposite rotation"]],["FIGCAPTION",{},"Illustrative engineering diagram. Not to scale; no flight telemetry or numerical simulation."]],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"A linked design problem"],["P",{},"Large, rapidly turning blades and a lightweight vehicle help address the thin atmosphere. These choices work together. Lower gravity helps; it does not make a heavy vehicle with small, slow blades a safe substitute."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","The diagram shows relationships, not a calculator for real flight performance. No numerical flight physics is simulated."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]],["BUTTON",{"class":"text-button"},"Collect evidence: Less air, less lift"]]],["DETAILS",{"class":"evidence-card","data-collected":"false"},["SUMMARY",{},"Two rotors, opposite directions",["SMALL",{},"Open record"]],["DIV",{"class":"evidence-body"},["P",{"class":"record-context"},"Rotor system · lift and control"],["P",{},"Two stacked rotors turn in opposite directions. Their opposing torques help prevent the body from simply spinning the other way. The blades are carbon-fibre structures, not solid heavy metal paddles."],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"Control is more than speed"],["P",{},"Ingenuity controls flight by adjusting blade pitch: the angle at which blades meet the air. That changes lift and allows control of the aircraft. It is misleading to treat it as a consumer drone controlled only by changing motor speeds."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","Lift, torque and control solve different parts of the flight problem. The static model shows the engineering arrangement, not a running rotor simulation."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]],["P",{"class":"record-requirement"},"First inspect ","Counter-rotating rotors"," using its existing hotspot or component list above."],["BUTTON",{"class":"text-button","disabled":""},"Collect evidence: Two rotors, opposite directions"]]]],["DIV",{"class":"evidence-listen"},[[60,227]],["DETAILS",{"class":"listen-mode"},["SUMMARY",{},["svg",{"aria-hidden":"true","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","width":"22","height":"22"},["path",{"d":"M4 15V9a8 8 0 0116 0v6l-3 5H7zM7 8h10v7H7z","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"1.5"}]]," Helmet Listen Mode"],["P",{},"Listen to ","Less air, less lift",". Original text stays available. Browser voices vary; word-by-word synchronization is not provided."],["P",{},"Audio is muted. ",["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Unmute audio"]],["DIV",{"class":"listen-controls"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Listen / Replay"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","disabled":""},"Pause narration"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Stop narration"]],["LABEL",{"for":"_r_8_"},"Narration speed"],["SELECT",{"id":"_r_8_"},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"0.75"},"0.75","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"true","value":"1"},"1","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.25"},"1.25","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.5"},"1.5","×"]],["LABEL",{},"Voice volume",["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"1","aria-label":"Voice volume","min":"0","max":"1","step":"0.1","type":"range","value":"1"}]],["P