l. The rover no longer supplied power through the old physical connection. Ingenuity needed to recharge and manage its own heat."]],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"A careful trade-off"],["P",{},"Keeping the interior warmer consumes energy. Turning off essential protection to maximise flying time is not a sound survival strategy. Flight preparation also depends on temperatures and available charge."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","“It landed” and “it can survive until tomorrow” are different conclusions. Neither should be assumed from the other."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]],["BUTTON",{"class":"text-button"},"Collect evidence: Landing was not the end of the day"]]]],["DIV",{"class":"evidence-listen"},[[109,227]],["DETAILS",{"class":"listen-mode"},["SUMMARY",{},["svg",{"aria-hidden":"true","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","width":"22","height":"22"},["path",{"d":"M4 15V9a8 8 0 0116 0v6l-3 5H7zM7 8h10v7H7z","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"1.5"}]]," Helmet Listen Mode"],["P",{},"Listen to ","Daylight has another job",". Original text stays available. Browser voices vary; word-by-word synchronization is not provided."],["P",{},"Audio is muted. ",["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Unmute audio"]],["DIV",{"class":"listen-controls"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Listen / Replay"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","disabled":""},"Pause narration"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Stop narration"]],["LABEL",{"for":"_r_a_"},"Narration speed"],["SELECT",{"id":"_r